<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* No static <title> here: every page supplies its own through <PageTitle>, and with
       prerendering the HeadOutlet emits a real <title> element into this head. *@
    <meta name="description" content="bit Bortable (Bit.Bortable) - a Blazor-native drag-and-drop sortable list inspired by SortableJS: reorder items, drag them between lists, clone, swap and multi-drag, with the sorting engine written in C#." />

    @* Link previews: the card a chat client or a social site unfurls is the first impression a
       shared link makes. *@
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Bit.Bortable" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Bortable - drag-and-drop sortable lists for Blazor" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Reorder items, drag them between lists, clone, swap and multi-drag - with the sorting engine written in C#, not a JavaScript wrapper." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />

    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* The site kit (app.css, theme.js, site.js - shared by every Utilities demo), then this demo's
       own sample styles. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["demo.css"]" />
    @* The library's stylesheet. Unlike its script, it is not loaded on demand: without it the drag states -
       the ghost, the hidden original of an item previewed in another list, the swap target, the multi-drag
       selection - are not drawn. It comes after demo.css so its state rules win over the demo's item styles. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Bit.Bortable/bit-bortable.css"]" />
    @* Scoped-CSS bundle: includes the client project's *.razor.css files as well. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Bit.Bortable.Demo.Server.styles.css"]" />
    @* Synchronous on purpose: applies the light/dark theme before first paint. *@
    <script src="@Assets["theme.js"]"></script>
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
</head>

<body>
    @* InteractiveWebAssembly rather than Auto or Server: every dragover of a drag is handled in C#, and on
       WebAssembly none of them waits on a network round trip. The pages are still prerendered, so the first
       response carries the lists. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
    <div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
        <span class="dismiss">&#128473;</span>
    </div>
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["site.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
